---
import { Picture } from "astro:assets";
import { Icon } from "astro-icon/components";
import construction from "../assets/construction/mta-precast-wall.jpg";
import credit from "../assets/construction/ATTRIBUTION.json";
---

<div class="construction-context wide">
  <figure class="construction-photo">
    <div class="construction-photo-label">
      Construction context · Precast installation
    </div>
    <a
      class="construction-photo-link"
      href={construction.src}
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener"
      aria-label="Open the construction photograph in a new tab: workers beside a suspended precast wall"
    >
      <Picture
        src={construction}
        alt="A precast concrete wall section hangs from a lifting machine's hook and slings beside workers inside the West Cavern Terminal. The equipment supports the wall while the crew works at its installation position."
        formats={["webp"]}
        widths={[640, 960, 1440, 2000]}
        sizes="(max-width: 760px) 92vw, 720px"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <span class="figure-expand" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
    </a>
    <figcaption>
      Precast platform-wall installation, West Cavern Terminal, 2017.<br />
      Photo: <a href={credit.source}>{credit.creator}</a> · <a
        href={credit.licenseUrl}>CC BY 2.0</a
      >. Resized and compressed for the web; image content unchanged.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
  <div class="construction-question">
    <span class="eyebrow">From construction to robotics</span>
    <h3>Can a humanoid learn to guide the load?</h3>
    <p>
      Supporting a load and placing it precisely are different tasks. A
      suspended element must be guided toward its target while its motion
      settles.
    </p>
    <p>
      HOIST studies the guidance problem: coordinating whole-body movement,
      contact, and stopping as an externally supported payload descends.
    </p>
    <p class="construction-scope">
      <strong>Our testbed.</strong> Simulation and a laboratory humanoid with a 2.5
      kg suspended box. The construction photograph illustrates the motivation; the
      experiments evaluate this controlled task.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<aside class="industry-resources" aria-labelledby="industry-resources-title">
  <h3 id="industry-resources-title">See the work on site</h3>
  <p>
    Industry examples show the steps around a lift: guiding an element, aligning
    it, and making its connections.
  </p>
  <div class="industry-video-links">
    <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-X3LcfsuGhE">
      <Icon name="ri:play-circle-line" aria-hidden="true" />
      <span
        ><strong>Precast column installation</strong><span
          >Peikko · Watch on YouTube</span
        ></span
      >
      <span class="industry-link-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
    </a>
    <a href="https://www.nccbuilt.com/videos">
      <Icon name="ri:play-circle-line" aria-hidden="true" />
      <span
        ><strong>Floor-module lifting and placement</strong><span
          >NCC · Watch on the producer’s website</span
        ></span
      >
      <span class="industry-link-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
    </a>
  </div>
</aside>
